0..45 Comment "// This source shows the prelude `Ord` model."
46..48 Comment "//"
49..125 Comment "// The integer and string models order values of their carrier. `OrdInteger`"
126..205 Comment "// answers with the integer primitives, so its verdicts are theirs. `OrdString`"
206..275 Comment "// orders strings byte by byte, as a Rust `BTreeMap<String, _>` does."
276..278 Comment "//"
279..355 Comment "// The checker resolves each comparison from the operand type. The operators"
356..436 Comment "// `<`, `<=`, `>` and `>=` call the prelude functions `lt`, `le`, `gt` and `ge`."
437..513 Comment "// Each `Ord` model includes its `Eq` model. So `==` still resolves at both."
514..516 Comment "//"
517..532 Comment "// - see: #2333"
